.TH NETD 8 "October 2026" "Peios netd 0.1.8" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
netd \- reconcile Peios network state from the registry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/sbin/netd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netd
is the Peios network manager and the executor of Peios Network Policy's
interface layer. It reads desired state below
.BR Machine\eSystem\eNetwork ,
observes links over rtnetlink, and owns links, addresses, routes, DHCP, router
discovery, and the network inventory for interfaces policy tells it to join.
.PP
The daemon runs as SYSTEM because current Peios network-administration and raw
packet privileges are held by that identity. Its service publishes the
.B network
role and readiness levels
.BR link ,
.BR addressed ,
and
.BR routed .
.PP
Configuration is declarative. Manual changes to a joined interface can be
reverted at the next reconciliation. An interface whose policy verdict is
.B IGNORE
is not touched.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/netd/control.sock
Control and status object used by
.BR net (1)
and the resolver integration.
.TP
.I /var/state/netd
Persistent network and interface identity state.
.TP
.I /usr/share/regman/netd.regman
Machine-readable registry reference installed by the package.
.SH SECURITY
Query and control operations are authorized against the descriptor stored in
.B Machine\eSystem\eNetwork ControlSecurity.
The compiled default allows everyone to query and restricts control to SYSTEM
and Administrators. Registry Status keys written by netd are protected from
operator writes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR net (1),
.BR reg (1),
.BR regman (1)
